        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Austria, Vienna, Graz, Slovenia, Spielfeld, Semmering, Bruck an der Mur, Gloggnitz, Mürzzuschlag, Wien Liesing railway station\n- Systems: Southern Railway, Semmering railway\n\nFacts:\n- Wien Liesing railway station opened in 1841 together with the Southern Railway.\n- The Southern Railway is a railway in Austria that runs from Vienna to Graz and to the Slovenia border at Spielfeld via Semmering and Bruck an der Mur.\n- The Semmering railway in Austria starts at Gloggnitz and leads over the Semmering to Mürzzuschlag.\n- The Semmering railway was the first mountain railway in Europe built with a standard-gauge track.",
